<X3D profile='Interchange' version='4.1' xmlns:xsd='http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance' xsd:noNamespaceSchemaLocation='https://www.web3d.org/specifications/x3d-4.1.xsd'>
<head><component name='Shape' level='5'/><component name='Lighting' level='3'/><component name='Rendering' level='3'/><component name='Shaders' level='1'/><component name='CubeMapTexturing' level='1'/><component name='PointingDeviceSensor' level='1'/><component name='Grouping' level='2'/><meta name='title' content='Torso CT (lite)'/><meta name='description' content='Whole-body CT of one subject as translucent glass anatomy with a glowing heart, vessels and brain. ILLUSTRATIVE rendering of real segmentation data.'/><meta name='creator' content='x3d.brain torso builder'/><meta name='rights' content='Derived from TotalSegmentator example subject s1397; attribution Wasserthal et al. 2023 (doi 10.1148/ryai.230024); license grade Likely (not Confirmed): CC BY 4.0, inferred from the dataset&apos;s published terms, licence record of this copy not read'/><meta name='variant' content='lite'/><meta name='synthetic' content='Look (glow, halos, colours) is ILLUSTRATIVE; geometry is derived from real CT segmentation of one subject'/></head>
<Scene>
<WorldInfo DEF='WORLD' title='Torso CT (lite)' info='"Torso CT (lite)" "Subject: TotalSegmentator example subject s1397 (whole-body CT, 117 binary segmentations), resampled to 3 mm voxels, distributed with the pyvista example data (Apache-2.0 repository)." "Data attribution: Wasserthal J. et al., TotalSegmentator, Radiology: Artificial Intelligence 2023, doi 10.1148/ryai.230024. License grade LIKELY, not Confirmed: CC BY 4.0, inferred from the dataset&apos;s published terms; the licence record of this copy was not read." "Derived content: smoothed and decimated surface meshes (signed-distance field, marching cubes, Taubin smoothing, quadric decimation). Changes were made. No raw CT or segmentation volumes are included." "Skin = threshold of the subject CT (HU above -300, largest component, holes filled). Lung vessels = iso-surface of the CT (smoothed, 0.6 voxel) inside the lung masks (HU above -470): threshold-derived, includes airway walls; not a vessel segmentation." "Brain ghost: template cortex (fsaverage, FreeSurfer lineage, license grade SUSPECTED, decimated here to about 3,000 vertices per hemisphere in the lite scene; Fischl et al. 1999) plus aseg cerebellum and brainstem (MNI152NLin2009cAsym, Fonov et al. 2011), affinely fitted into this subject&apos;s brain mask (ICP, mean two-way surface distance 10.3 mm). ILLUSTRATIVE: the folds are the template&apos;s, not this subject&apos;s. The subject&apos;s own brain segmentation (3 mm, no folds) is in SW_BRAIN_CT, hidden by default." "The subject has a pronounced forward head posture and raised arms; shown as recorded. Skin above the shoulders fades out on the lateral arms for clarity." "Glow, halos, colours and the translucent look are artistic rendering choices, not tissue properties. ILLUSTRATIVE; not for diagnosis." "Frame: X patient-right, Y up, Z posterior; 1 unit = 1 mm; origin at x=239.25 y=210.0 z=410.0 mm of the data frame." "Builder: build_torso_scene.py, variant lite, builder sha256 23cea36ce451fdc9"'/>
